-- #822: two graded interfaces that spell their row-indexed head the SAME way (`f`)
-- but put the Row in DIFFERENT slots.  Both must declare cleanly and independently.
--
-- ⚠️ This fixture asserted the OPPOSITE until the adversarial review of PR #1011.
-- The first cut of #822 keyed the graded kinds by the bare type-parameter NAME, so
-- the two collided; the fixture pinned that they then "degrade loudly" and called
-- that degradation deliberate.  It was not deliberate, it was a symptom — and the
-- claim was false anyway: ACROSS MODULES the loser depended on the order of two
-- import lines in a third file.  The scope now travels as an argument
-- (gradedScopeOf), so there is no shared key left to collide over.
interface GA f where
  ga : f e a -> (a -> <e> f e b) -> f e b

interface GB f where
  gb : f a e -> (a -> <e> f a e) -> f a e
